a:112:{s:12:"allegederror";s:17:"Erreur présumée";s:20:"allegederror_details";s:24:"Erreur présumée ({$a})";s:18:"allegederrorplural";s:19:"Erreurs présumées";s:10:"almostsure";s:12:"Presque sûr";s:18:"almostsure_details";s:24:"vous étiez presque sûr";s:6:"answer";s:26:"votre réponse était {$a}";s:21:"answercategorydetails";s:35:"{$a->certainty} et {$a->youranswer}";s:18:"answersrepartition";s:19:"Answers repartition";s:17:"attemptsevolution";s:18:"Attempts evolution";s:12:"attempttitle";s:55:"Attempt {$a->num} of {$a->attemptcount} from {$a->date}";s:16:"behavioursummary";s:33:"Résumé des niveaux de certitude";s:15:"clickfordetails";s:19:"(Click for details)";s:14:"confidencerate";s:15:"Confidence rate";s:19:"confidencerate_help";s:389:"<p>Indicates the mean certainty level of correct answers (not counting random answers). Ideally, it should be a rather high value, as you should be quite sure of your correct answers. If it is rather low, it means that your knowledge is unsecure. In the event that you have no correct answer, the confidence rate is not computed.</p><div><b>Value:</b> between {$a->min} and {$a->max}</div>";s:19:"confidencerate_nodi";s:15:"Confidence rate";s:24:"confidencerate_nodi_help";s:359:"<p>Indicates the mean certainty level of correct answers. Ideally, it should be a rather high value, as you should be quite sure of your correct answers. If it is rather low, it means that your knowledge is unsecure. In the event that you have no correct answer, the confidence rate is not computed.</p><div><b>Value:</b> between {$a->min} and {$a->max}</div>";s:15:"confidenceratea";s:21:"Confidence rate: {$a}";s:7:"correct";s:8:"correcte";s:14:"correctanswers";s:19:"Réponses correctes";s:17:"declaredignorance";s:18:"Réponse au hasard";s:25:"declaredignorance_details";s:109:"Réponse au hasard (vous avez répondu au hasard, peu importe que votre réponse soit correcte ou incorrecte)";s:23:"declaredignoranceplural";s:19:"Réponses au hasard";s:21:"declaredignorancerate";s:23:"Declared ignorance rate";s:26:"declaredignorancerate_help";s:321:"<p>Indicates the percentage of questions where you answered giving the minimal certainty level "{$a}", which is interpreted as a "random" answer. Answers associated with this "declared ignorance" certainty level are not taken into account in other metacognitive indicators.</p><div><b>Value:</b> between 0% and 100%</div>";s:22:"declaredignoranceratea";s:29:"Declared ignorance rate: {$a}";s:26:"declaredignorancerateabove";s:29:"Declared ignorance above {$a}";s:26:"declaredignoranceratebelow";s:29:"Declared ignorance below {$a}";s:13:"expectedtrend";s:17:"Tendance attendue";s:18:"expectedtrend_help";s:229:"Cette courbe décrit la forme globale que l’histogramme prendrait pour un comportement lucide. Plus l’histogramme est proche de la forme de cette courbe, plus vous étiez lucide vis-à-vis de vos réponses et votre certitude.";s:13:"gradeover100a";s:15:"Grade: {$a}/100";s:14:"imprudencerate";s:15:"Imprudence rate";s:19:"imprudencerate_help";s:403:"<p>Indicates the mean certainty level of incorrect answers (not counting random answers). Ideally, it should be a rather low value, as you should be doubtful about your incorrect answers. If it is rather high, it means that you do not expect your own errors. In the event that you have no incorrect answer, the imprudence rate is not computed.</p><div><b>Value:</b> between {$a->min} and {$a->max}</div>";s:19:"imprudencerate_nodi";s:15:"Imprudence rate";s:24:"imprudencerate_nodi_help";s:373:"<p>Indicates the mean certainty level of incorrect answers. Ideally, it should be a rather low value, as you should be doubtful about your incorrect answers. If it is rather high, it means that you do not expect your own errors. In the event that you have no incorrect answer, the imprudence rate is not computed.</p><div><b>Value:</b> between {$a->min} and {$a->max}</div>";s:15:"imprudenceratea";s:21:"Imprudence rate: {$a}";s:9:"incorrect";s:10:"incorrecte";s:16:"incorrectanswers";s:21:"Réponses incorrectes";s:13:"lucidityindex";s:14:"Lucidity index";s:18:"lucidityindex_help";s:727:"<p>Index computed as the mean certainty level for correct answers (counted positively, excluding random answers) weighted by the proportion of correct answers, minus the mean certainty level for incorrect answers (counted negatively, excluding random answers) weighted by the proportion of incorrect answers. If this lucidity index is openly positive, it means that you are rather sure of your correct answers and unsure of your incorrect answers. If it is openly negative, this indicates a problem as you seem more sure about your incorrect answers than your correct ones! If it is around 0, it means that you are as sure about your correct answers than your incorrect answers.</p><div><b>Value:</b> between -100 and 100</div>";s:18:"lucidityindex_nodi";s:14:"Lucidity index";s:23:"lucidityindex_nodi_help";s:675:"<p>Index computed as the mean certainty level for correct answers (counted positively) weighted by the proportion of correct answers, minus the mean certainty level for incorrect answers (counted negatively) weighted by the proportion of incorrect answers. If this lucidity index is openly positive, it means that you are rather sure of your correct answers and unsure of your incorrect answers. If it is openly negative, this indicates a problem as you seem more sure about your incorrect answers than your correct ones! If it is around 0, it means that you are as sure about your correct answers than your incorrect answers.</p><div><b>Value:</b> between -100 and 100</div>";s:14:"lucidityindexa";s:20:"Lucidity index: {$a}";s:29:"lucidityindicatorallegederror";s:51:"No unexpected error, but at least one alleged error";s:34:"lucidityindicatordeclaredignorance";s:36:"All questions are answered at random";s:30:"lucidityindicatorsureknowledge";s:38:"All answers are well-founded knowledge";s:32:"lucidityindicatorunexpectederror";s:29:"At least one unexpected error";s:32:"lucidityindicatorunsureknowledge";s:45:"No error, but at least one unsecure knowledge";s:22:"metacognitiveindicator";s:23:"Metacognitive indicator";s:23:"metacognitiveindicators";s:24:"Metacognitive indicators";s:15:"ncorrectanswers";s:27:"Réponses correctes : {$a}";s:18:"ndeclaredignorance";s:27:"Réponses au hasard : {$a}";s:17:"nincorrectanswers";s:29:"Réponses incorrectes : {$a}";s:14:"noallegederror";s:17:"No presumed error";s:19:"nodeclaredignorance";s:16:"No random answer";s:15:"nosureknowledge";s:25:"No well-founded knowledge";s:17:"nounexpectederror";s:19:"No unexpected error";s:17:"nounsureknowledge";s:21:"No unsecure knowledge";s:12:"numofanswers";s:19:"Nombre de réponses";s:13:"otherattempts";s:14:"Other attempts";s:21:"pleaseselectcertainty";s:38:"Veuillez sélectionner une catégorie.";s:10:"pluginname";s:61:"Niveaux de certitude et feedback de l’étudiant (différé)";s:14:"pluginsettings";s:56:"Paramètres des comportements avec degrés de certitudes";s:21:"privacy:behaviourpath";s:9:"Behaviour";s:32:"privacy:metadata:attemptstepdata";s:60:"This plugin stores some data submitted during quiz attempts.";s:21:"privacy:metadata:name";s:92:"Attempt step data variable name, among [certainty, studentfeedback, generalstudentfeedback].";s:22:"privacy:metadata:value";s:384:"Attempt step data variable value.For certainty, certainty that submitted answer would be considered correct, for each attempted question using this behaviour.For studentfeedback, feedback submitted after a question attempt, for each attempted question using this behaviour.For generalstudentfeedback, global feedback submitted after a quiz attempt, for each quiz using this behaviour.";s:9:"quitesure";s:12:"Plutôt sûr";s:17:"quitesure_details";s:24:"vous étiez plutôt sûr";s:11:"quiteunsure";s:8:"Peu sûr";s:19:"quiteunsure_details";s:20:"vous étiez peu sûr";s:6:"random";s:20:"Fifty-fifty ou moins";s:10:"random_alt";s:25:"J’ai répondu au hasard";s:14:"random_details";s:28:"vous avez répondu au hasard";s:11:"random_open";s:25:"Je pense que c’est faux";s:29:"settings:answercategorization";s:29:"Catégorisation des réponses";s:22:"settings:answerclasses";s:20:"Classes de réponses";s:26:"settings:answerclassesinfo";s:216:"Vous pouvez personnaliser la couleur associée à chaque classe de réponses.<br>
Vous pouvez modifier le nom affiché des classes de réponses via <a href="{$a}">les paramètres de personnalisation de la langue</a>.";s:24:"settings:certaintylevela";s:25:"Degré de certitude {$a}";s:24:"settings:certaintylevels";s:20:"Degrés de certitude";s:28:"settings:certaintylevelsinfo";s:365:"Vous pouvez personnaliser le nom affiché (si pertinent), le pourcentage affiché ainsi que la manière dont sera catégorisée chaque réponse selon qu’elle est vraie / fausse, pour chaque degré de certitude.<br>
Vous pouvez modifier plus finement le nom affiché des degrés de certitude via <a href="{$a}">les paramètres de personnalisation de la langue</a>.";s:27:"settings:enablefbforclasses";s:72:"Afficher le champ de commentaire étudiant pour les classes de réponses";s:32:"settings:enablefbforclasses_help";s:176:"Le champ proposant à l’étudiant d’écrire un commentaire à propos de sa réponse ne sera affiché que pour les réponses appartenant aux classifications sélectionnées.";s:28:"settings:error:categoryorder";s:276:"Veuillez conserver une continuité entre les catégorisations de degrés de certitude : d’abord un degré optionnel de Réponse au hasard, puis les degrés de Connaissance fragile / Erreurs présumées, et enfin les degrés de Connaissance solide / Erreurs insoupçonnées.";s:14:"settings:label";s:12:"Nom affiché";s:20:"settings:loadpresets";s:36:"Charger le préréglage d’échelle";s:19:"settings:percentage";s:11:"Pourcentage";s:27:"settings:preset:alternative";s:22:"Alternatif (linéaire)";s:23:"settings:preset:default";s:25:"Défaut (<em>legacy</em>)";s:27:"settings:preset:recommended";s:27:"Recommandé (non-linéaire)";s:24:"settings:studentfeedback";s:30:"Champ de commentaire étudiant";s:21:"settings:useopenlabel";s:68:"le nom alternatif de degré de certitude pour les questions ouvertes";s:26:"settings:useopenlabel_help";s:155:"Pour les questions ouvertes (i.e. ni Vrai/Faux ni Questions à choix multiple), ce nom alternatif peut être utilisé pour décrire ce degré de certitude.";s:22:"settings:useopenlabela";s:49:"Utiliser « {$a} » pour les questions ouvertes";s:18:"settingsformerrors";s:152:"Modifications non enregistrées. Des erreurs ont été trouvées dans les données envoyées. Veuillez vous référer aux messages d’erreur ci-après.";s:15:"showthatattempt";s:17:"Show that attempt";s:4:"sure";s:17:"Tout à fait sûr";s:12:"sure_details";s:29:"vous étiez tout à fait sûr";s:13:"sureknowledge";s:19:"Connaissance solide";s:21:"sureknowledge_details";s:26:"Connaissance solide ({$a})";s:19:"sureknowledgeplural";s:21:"Connaissances solides";s:11:"thisattempt";s:23:"This attempt (no. {$a})";s:17:"thisattemptdetail";s:34:"Detail for this attempt (no. {$a})";s:15:"unexpectederror";s:21:"Erreur insoupçonnée";s:23:"unexpectederror_details";s:28:"Erreur insoupçonnée ({$a})";s:21:"unexpectederrorplural";s:23:"Erreurs insoupçonnées";s:6:"unsure";s:14:"Très peu sûr";s:14:"unsure_details";s:26:"vous étiez très peu sûr";s:15:"unsureknowledge";s:20:"Connaissance fragile";s:23:"unsureknowledge_details";s:27:"Connaissance fragile ({$a})";s:21:"unsureknowledgeplural";s:22:"Connaissances fragiles";s:16:"viewcoursereport";s:35:"View evolution along course quizzes";s:24:"whatisyourcertaintylevel";s:64:"Quel est votre degré de certitude associé à votre réponse ?";}